{"step_index":2622,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T11:38:14Z","input_tokens":3381,"cache_read_tokens":109095,"output_tokens":6373,"thinking":"Initializing the `DsaDashboard` component involves setting default states for its sub-tab, the currently active topic detail, and various filters. These filters include search query, selected topic, difficulty, pattern, and status, all initialized to their default 'all' state.\n\n\nThe component's state variables are being initialized to manage problem filtering and sorting. Added settings for roadmap stage management, including a function to load the active stage from local storage and another to set and persist it.  A function `getStageProblems` is added to filter problems relevant to a specified stage by matching topics.\n\n\nCalculating stage statistics involves filtering problems by stage topics. Determining the total, solved, attempted, and not-started counts is necessary.  The completion percentage and milestone solved status are also factors.\n\nI need to classify the stage completion status according to the rules: 'not_started', 'mastered', or 'in_progress'.  The logic seems correct, but should double-check the 'mastered' condition to ensure it covers all scenarios.\n\n\nThe stage completion status is classified based on these conditions: \"mastered\" if either zero problems exist, or if at least 5 problems are solved and the completion percentage is at least 50% and the milestone is also solved. \"in\\_progress\" if there are any solved or attempted problems. Otherwise, the status is \"not\\_started\". Now need to implement functions `practiceNextInStage` and `exploreStageProblems`.\nThe next unsolved problem in a stage will be opened in a workspace if present, otherwise, the stage's milestone problem will be opened.\n\nThe `exploreStageProblems` function is designed to configure filters for exploring problems related to a specific stage.\n\n\nThe function `renderRoadmapOverviewCard` needs to generate the HTML for displaying the roadmap overview. It iterates through each stage, calculating stage statistics to determine completion status and progress. I'll need to use these stats to dynamically render the item's appearance, incl\n<truncated 2869 bytes>\nng badges for difficulty and LeetCode number, along with the problem title and pattern. Visual indicators for solved or attempted status are also included. Action buttons are added to open a full workspace. Currently, I'm inspecting the output for accuracy.\n\n\nThe roadmap overview card now renders HTML for each stage. It incorporates a progress bar reflecting problem-solving progress and difficulty distribution. A milestone banner is included, which shows the milestone problem's status and links to a workspace.\n\nThe roadmap cards feature recommended starter problems for quick practice initiation.  Dynamic HTML generation for each starter problem chip is implemented, along with difficulty and LeetCode number badges. Visual indicators and workspace action buttons are also included.\n\n\nThe generated HTML for the roadmap overview card now incorporates starter problems within each stage. I am dynamically producing the starter problem chips, including difficulty and LeetCode badges. Visual cues and buttons for workspace interaction are also integrated. The rendering of these components is under review.\n\n\nOverall progress statistics are calculated across all stages. The roadmap now includes quick jump navigation with stage status icons.  Roadmap cards are being generated dynamically, reflecting stage completion.\n\nDynamic completion status application is being applied to each roadmap card, enhancing the visual clarity. The code is structured to iterate through the data to create a display.\n\nThe HTML for each roadmap card is being generated, using calculated statistics.  Completion status badges and topic chips are being included. Action buttons for stage focus are also incorporated.\n\n\nThe full roadmap and the roadmap timeline-only views are being rendered, and statistics are computed. The `renderRoadmapTimelineOnly` function is implemented to update a specific container with the full roadmap view using the computed stats. The code verifies `DsaDashboard` and other relevant data are exposed to the global `window` object.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/index.html\"","EndLine":"90","StartLine":"50","toolAction":"\"Viewing tab buttons in index.html\"","toolSummary":"\"View tab buttons in index.html\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
